OL,3,GNEWSAFarmers grieving over bluetongue
OL,4,Aurged to talk
OL,5,
OL,6,FFarmers and support workers say
OL,7,Fbluetongue has hit agriculture hard and
OL,8,Ffear it will have a "lasting impact".
OL,10,FSouth-west England has been
OL,11,Fparticularly badly affected by the
OL,12,Fvirus. Farmers who have lost animals to
OL,13,Fthe virus are feeling "a tremendous
OL,14,Fsense of grief", said Andy Jerrard, the
OL,15,FMethodist Church's rural support
OL,16,Fworker.
OL,18,FJerry Sanders-Carr, who runs Exe Valley
OL,19,FLamb, near Exeter, and has lost 15% of
OL,20,Fhis sheep to bluetongue said farmers
OL,21,Fwere offering each other support.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,346,340,200,160,0,100
